      "problem": "Find the greatest common divisor of $1\\,518$ and $286.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}1\\,518 & = & 286(5) & + & 88 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 286 & = & 88(3) & + & 22 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 88 & = & 22(4) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $22.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $1\\,518$ and $286$ is $22.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(1\\,518,286)=22.\n$$",
